  "articleBody": "Bathroom floors endure heavy moisture, foot traffic, and humidity swings. While cosmetic wear is easy to spot, structural and moisture issues require immediate contractor intervention before hidden damage spreads.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nReach out to an experienced general contractor if you notice any of these warning signs:\n- The floor feels spongy, springs underfoot, or dips near the toilet base or tub apron.\n- Cracked grout lines keep reappearing even after you re-grout, indicating excessive subfloor deflection.\n- Tiles are lifting, rocking, or sounding hollow when tapped, pointing to failed bonding or trapped water.\n- You detect persistent musty odors that linger despite frequent surface cleaning.\n- Water has leaked through the ceiling below your second-story bathroom.\n\nA failing bathroom floor often hides rotted joists, swollen underlayment, or leaking supply lines. Simply laying new vinyl or tile over damaged wood traps decay, leading to costly structural repairs later. \n\nAbraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC brings hands-on framing, tile installation, and general contracting experience to every project. Serving Aurora, Denver, and surrounding communities, our crew handles complete teardowns, subfloor repairs, and finish tile work. Call 303-505-0866 to schedule an inspection.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
